00:43:46.000 --> 00:44:24.000
The British begin to prevail on the battlefield. Kitchener, first Lord Roberts, and then Kitchener come in to conduct the war in a much more ruthless way. They end up herding the Boers, Boer civilians, into concentration camps so that they can basically starve out the guerrillas. And it then becomes an attritional, very bloody, sort of dirty campaign. And Churchill doesn't really like it. Your characterization, I completely agree with. So Churchill has this motto, in war, resolution, in defeat, defiance, in victory, magnanimity, in peace, goodwill.
